quant-4 (docs/research/deepinfer/quant-heads.md): online block-Hadamard-128 rotation of
the inputs of linears whose checkpoint weights are stored K-rotated, behind
VLLM_ACT_HADAMARD_RE=<regex of layer prefixes> (default unset = off, no code path
changes).

A matching CompressedTensorsWNA16 layer must run on MarlinLinearKernel with
K % 128 == 0 (else ValueError at load). MarlinLinearKernel.apply_weights then computes
x' = x . blockdiag(H_pm1 / 8) (one batched bf16 matmul, fp32 accumulate, exact
factors) and feeds x' to the unchanged apply_gptq_marlin_linear, so both the W4A16
path and the W4A8-int8 path (per_token_quant_int8 on x') see the rotated input.
The checkpoint carries W' = W . blockdiag(H_pm1) / 16, so x' . W'^T == x . W^T;
build it with docs/research/deepinfer/experiments/quant4_h128down.py. Pointing the
knob at layers of an unrotated checkpoint gives wrong outputs.

Adds VLLM_ACT_HADAMARD_RE to envs.py (hashed into the torch.compile cache key).
Touches only hunks the image's own syv patches do not; applies on the stock image,
with or without quant2-lossless-fold.patch. Test: bench/test_act_hadamard.py.

Apply: patch -p1 --forward --fuzz 0 -d /app/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < quant4-act-hadamard.patch

